Farzana Iqbal was stoned to death here  outside the High Court building in  Lahore allegedly by members of her own  family  police say the 25 year old and her  husband were waiting for the court to  open when around a dozen men attacked  her with bricks the local police chief  said she was killed because she refused  to accept an arranged marriage with her  cousin she married the man she loved her  parents filed an abduction case against  them they were here for their case in  the High Court the incident happened on  their way to court her family stoned her  to death  lisanna suffered severe head injuries  and was taken to hospital but was  pronounced dead on arrival  her husband escaped injury Farzana is  said to have been three months pregnant  police say her father two brothers and  former fiance were among the attackers  her father turned himself in to the  police saying the killing was a matter  of Honor Pakistani authorities say  nearly nine hundred women were murdered  in so-called honour killings in 2013  human rights groups say many cases go  unreported and the real number may be  much higher
 

